    "q-97687": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97687",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Lucy's marbles are labeled with numbers $0$ through $9.$ If Lucy chooses a marble at random, what is the standard deviation of the numbers of the selected marbles? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the number of the chosen marble. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{0,1,…,9\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{SD}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then the variance of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{|S{|}^{2}-1}{12}\n$$\n\nwhere $S=\\{a,a+1,…,b\\}.$\n\nNow, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S| & =b-a+1 \\\\  & =9-0+1 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{0,1,…,9\\},$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{{10}^{2}-1}{12}=\\frac{99}{12}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{99}{12}}≈2.87.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
