    "q-97662": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97662",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Jack wants to buy a single issue of a particular comic series with $55$ issues. Unfortunately, the comic store does not have the first $7$ issues in stock. If Jack buys a comic at random from the available issues, what is the standard deviation of the issue numbers he could select? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the number of the issue Jack selects. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{8,9,…,55\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{SD}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then the variance of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{|S{|}^{2}-1}{12}\n$$\n\nwhere $S=\\{a,a+1,…,b\\}.$\n\nNow, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S| & =b-a+1 \\\\  & =55-8+1 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{8,9,…,55\\},$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{{48}^{2}-1}{12}=\\frac{2303}{12}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{2303}{12}}≈13.85.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
